To debug the Arm32 test program using the QEMU ARM simulator, do the following:

1. Click the debug icon in the left VS Code pane.
2. At the top of the left pane click to tiny "v" icon.
3. From the dropdown menu, select: Debug Arm32 Arm Baseline.
4. In the WSL cmd window go to folder ~/projects/Tics/Source/Target/Arm32.
5. Run the cmd below that starts with "arm-none-eabi-g++"
6. Now run the cmd below that starts with "qemu-system-arm"
7. In the current folder, open this file in the editor: Main.cpp.
8. Now press F5 to start the Debugger.
9. The Debugger will come up in main() and stop.
10. Press F5 to continue or F10 to single step.

Newset build command for Tics/Source/Target/Arm32
arm-none-eabi-g++ -mcpu=cortex-m3 -mthumb -O0 --specs=nano.specs --specs=nosys.specs -I../..  -ggdb3 -T./mps2_an385.ld ./Main.cpp ../../Tics.cpp ./Target.cpp ./Target.s -o ./ArmTest.elf

To fire up QEMU:
qemu-system-arm -machine mps2-an385 -cpu cortex-m3 -nographic -kernel ArmTest.elf -s -S

